  "description": "The (input, expected) pairs Fuaran.Core.Conformance.propagationEvalLaws draws from `seed` over `iterations` iterations (and dirtyPropagationLaws' fixed cyclic graph), computed by calling the pinned kit. A host reproduces the sample with its own ConfRng, one cursor across all iterations: per iteration draw intBelow(6) + 2 = n, the ids `0` .. `n-1`; for each node k ascending, intBelow(3) for each j < k ascending, k reading j where it is 0; intBelow(100) per node ascending, its base; intBelow(n), the changed node, whose base grows by 1000. Every input carries the graph as `deps` (each id to the ids it reads), so the vectors also replay without the draw. The evaluator is value(n) = base(n) + the sum of value(r) over n's declared reads r, a read that resolves to nothing counting 0. `dirtySet` expects the changed ids and every node that transitively reads one, sorted. `evaluationOrder` expects the order the reference walks — Tarjan over the ids in ascending ordinal order, each node's reads ascending, dependencies first — and the cyclic groups, each sorted; a host whose sort breaks ties differently instead holds its own order to the certificate: no id twice, order and cycles partitioning the ids, every acyclic read earlier. `evalFrom` re-evaluates `changedBase` incrementally over the prior `eval` of `base`: it expects the values, which equal a full evaluation of `changedBase`, and `recomputed`, the nodes the evaluator was invoked on, which is exactly the dirty set — or, for a changed id the graph does not hold, the evalUnknownChange refusal naming it. `undeclaredRead` makes `node` also read `read`, which it never declared: both eval and evalFrom (with `node` changed) refuse with evalUndeclaredRead naming the node and the read, whether the read names a node of the graph or an id it does not hold.",
